      "explanation": "Main idea: borgen can mean both to borrow and to lend, and the sentence determines the direction. borgen can mean both to borrow and to lend. The direction becomes clear from the person and the dative. If I take something from someone else, it is to borrow. If I give something to someone for a time, it is to lend. In everyday use, leihen, with a very similar meaning, is also often used. So borgen has to be read in context.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Kann ich mir dein Fahrrad borgen?",
          "lv": "Can I borrow your bike?"
        },
        {
          "de": "Ich borge dir mein Buch.",
          "lv": "I am lending you my book."
        },
        {
          "de": "Er borgt sich Geld von seinem Bruder.",
          "lv": "He is borrowing money from his brother."
        },
        {
          "de": "Sie borgt ihrer Freundin ein Kleid.",
          "lv": "She is lending her friend a dress."
        },
        {
          "de": "Darf ich mir einen Stift borgen?",
          "lv": "May I borrow a pen?"
        },
        {
          "de": "Wir borgen den Nachbarn die Leiter.",
          "lv": "We are lending the neighbours the ladder."
        }
      ],
      "comparison": [
        {
          "word": "borgen",
          "meaning": "to borrow / lend",
          "example": "Ich borge mir Geld. = I am borrowing money."
        },
        {
          "word": "leihen",
          "meaning": "to lend / borrow",
          "example": "Kannst du mir das Buch leihen? = Can you lend me the book?"
        },
        {
          "word": "geben",
          "meaning": "to give",
          "example": "Ich gebe dir Geld. = I am giving you money."
        },
        {
          "word": "zurückgeben",
          "meaning": "to give back",
          "example": "Ich gebe das Buch zurück. = I am giving the book back."
        }
      ],
      "tip": {
        "leftBlocks": [
          {
            "text": "mir borgen often means to borrow for yourself."
          },
          {
            "text": "dir/ihm borgen often means to lend to someone else."
          }
        ]
      },
      "important": {
        "text": "The meaning of borgen depends on the direction.",
        "example": "Ich borge mir etwas = I borrow something. Ich borge dir etwas = I lend you something."
      },
