      "explanation": [
        "Main idea: davor can mean a place in front, a time before that, or “of it” after fear or a warning.",
        "In space, davor means in front of something.",
        "In time, davor means before that.",
        "With fear or a warning, davor means of it.",
        "The context shows whether it is about place, time or reaction."
      ],
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Das Auto steht davor.",
          "lv": "The car is parked in front of it."
        },
        {
          "de": "Kurz davor war alles ruhig.",
          "lv": "Shortly before that everything was calm."
        },
        {
          "de": "Ich habe Angst davor.",
          "lv": "I am afraid of it."
        },
        {
          "de": "Er warnte mich davor.",
          "lv": "He warned me about it."
        },
        {
          "de": "Die Tür ist davor.",
          "lv": "The door is in front of it."
        },
        {
          "de": "Davor habe ich nichts gewusst.",
          "lv": "Before that I knew nothing."
        }
      ],
      "comparison": [
        {
          "word": "davor",
          "meaning": "in front / before that / of it",
          "example": "Ich habe Angst davor. = I am afraid of it."
        },
        {
          "word": "vor dem",
          "meaning": "before / in front of a specific thing",
          "example": "Vor dem Haus steht ein Auto. = A car is parked in front of the house."
        },
        {
          "word": "danach",
          "meaning": "after that",
          "example": "Danach gehen wir. = After that we are leaving."
        },
        {
          "word": "darauf",
          "meaning": "on it / after that",
          "example": "Ich warte darauf. = I am waiting for it."
        }
      ],
      "tip": [
        "If the sentence has fear or a warning, davor often means “of it”.",
        "If it is about time, davor means before that."
      ],
      "important": [
        "The meaning of davor changes with the context.",
        "vor dem is used with a specific noun.",
        "davor is not the same as danach."
      ],
