      "layout": "standardStudy",
      "translation": "Wood",
      "explanation": "Holz means wood or timber as a material. It is used for tables, furniture, boards and building timber. Holz can also mean firewood, when it is about a stove or heating. It is not a living tree in nature. A living tree is der Baum, but the material is Holz.",
      "examples": [
        {
          "de": "Der Tisch ist aus Holz.",
          "lv": "The table is made of wood."
        },
        {
          "de": "Wir brauchen Holz für den Ofen.",
          "lv": "We need wood for the stove."
        },
        {
          "de": "Trockenes Holz brennt gut.",
          "lv": "Dry wood burns well."
        },
        {
          "de": "Er schneidet Holz.",
          "lv": "He is sawing wood."
        },
        {
          "de": "Das Haus ist aus Holz gebaut.",
          "lv": "The house is built of wood."
        },
        {
          "de": "Im Wald stehen viele Bäume.",
          "lv": "There are lots of trees in the forest."
        }
      ],
      "tip": {
        "leftBlocks": [
          {
            "text": "If you can touch the material or something is made from it, use Holz."
          },
          {
            "text": "If it is about a living tree with leaves and branches, use der Baum."
          }
        ]
      },
      "important": {
        "text": "Holz is not a living tree.",
        "example": "A living tree = der Baum. Holz can also mean firewood."
      },
